CORE
Test
--function Test.main -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
JBMC initialises class literals by calling cproverInitializeClassLiteral of the
model of java.lang.Class. Its effects on static fields must persist: class
literals must thus only be initialised once all other static symbols
(including the static fields of java.lang.Class and the flag recording whether
its static initializer has run) have been initialised.
